    body: "On September 11th 2026, President University held its first day of MUN (PresMUN), attended by approximately 75 students from national and international universities. The United Nations General Assembly was one of the councils participating in this simulation.\n\nThe results revealed two opposing camps. In this case, they were divided into retentionists and abolitionists. Retentionists are pro-death penalty. They believe that the death penalty should be applied to serious cases such as premeditated murder, terrorism, or masterminding illegal trafficking. Retentionist countries include China, the United States, Iran, and Saudi Arabia.\n\nConversely, abolitionist countries are countries that reject the death penalty. They are anti-death penalty, do not implement it, or have abolished it in their respective countries.\n\nIn this session, a consensus was found on whether the death penalty should remain in force in all countries around the world."
